WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.740
Before you can fix something, you need to understand what's broken.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:09.980
In this case, what's broken is approximately everything. They say knowledge is power.

3
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:17.940
In this case, knowledge is mostly just depressing. But you need it, the way you need to know your house is on fire before

4
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:27.780
you can put it out. The Daily Body Count. Every day, 150,000 humans die from disease and aging.

5
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:35.540
That's fifty nine-elevens. Per day. Including weekends and holidays.

6
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.090
When one thing kills 3,000 people, it's a tragedy and you start wars.

7
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:47.820
When diseases kill 50 times that every day, it's called "natural causes," which is Latin for "you couldn't be bothered.".

8
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:54.000
After the first nine-eleven, America invaded two countries and spent two trillion dollars.

9
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:00.250
After the fifty daily nine-elevens, humanity shrugs and wonders what's for lunch.

10
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:07.880
Where the Money Goes. Killing each other: two point seven two trillion dollars per year.

11
00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:12.880
Curing diseases: sixty-seven point five billion dollars per year.

12
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.420
The real bottleneck isn't research funding. It's testing which treatments actually work.

13
00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:27.460
Governments worldwide spend four point five zero billion dollars annually on clinical trials versus two point seven two

14
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:37.190
trillion dollars on weapons. That's a 604 ratio, which in technical terms is called "having your priorities backwards.".

15
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:45.940
On Medical Research. Since 1970, the National Institutes of Health has spent over one trillion dollars studying diseases.

16
00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:55.400
Diseases cured: Zero. Of its forty-seven billion dollars annual budget, only three point three percent goes to actual drug

17
00:01:55.400 --> 00:02:02.660
trials in humans. The other ninety-seven percent goes to studying mice, building buildings, and publishing papers nobody

18
00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:08.020
reads. The system operates at two percent of its potential capacity to save lives.

19
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:15.880
On the F.D.A. The F.D.A. makes drugs eighty-two times more expensive than necessary.

20
00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:23.380
It takes 14 years and two point six zero billion dollars to get a drug from discovery to patient.

21
00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:31.620
That's longer than it took to build the pyramids. The pharaohs didn't have to file quarterly progress reports in triplicate.

22
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.640
Ninety-five percent of diseases have zero approved treatments because the F.D.A.

23
00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:43.860
is excellent at preventing any drugs from reaching people. On What War Costs.

24
00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:49.380
Humanity spends two point seven two trillion dollars every year on war.

25
00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:55.000
That works out to three hundred forty dollars per human on Earth for death tools.

26
00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:04.680
This budget includes: Nuclear bombs (13,000 of them, because 12,999 wouldn't destroy Earth thoroughly enough).

27
00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:11.700
Bullets (many). A.I. murder robots (the future is here and it's disappointing).

28
00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:19.900
Fighter jets that cost more than hospitals. Submarines (one submarine 1,000 cancer research labs).

29
00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:28.720
Probably some kind of earthquake machine. Your personal lifetime contribution to the murder budget is seventy-four thousand

30
00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.040
two hundred fifty-nine dollars. You could have bought a really nice casket instead.

31
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.320
Or, and this is just a thought, not needed a casket quite so soon.

32
00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:47.780
The interesting thing about having thirteen thousand nuclear warheads is that after the first few hundred, you're just showing

33
00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:55.940
off. You can only destroy Earth once. The remaining twelve thousand seven hundred are for what, exactly?

34
00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:02.320
Destroying Earth's ghost? It's like buying thirteen thousand fire extinguishers for a one-room flat.

35
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:10.000
At some point, the fire extinguishers are the fire hazard. On What Disease Costs.

36
00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:17.459
Disease extracts one hundred nine trillion dollars from humanity annually.

37
00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:26.260
That includes 10 million cancer deaths per year, 2 billion people with chronic diseases, and 1 billion depressed humans

38
00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:35.420
costing five trillion dollars in lost "wanting to exist.". If disease were a country, it would be the richest country on

39
00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:42.960
Earth by a factor of ten. Unfortunately, disease doesn't have a flag or an army, so nobody invades it.

40
00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:52.260
Out of two point four zero billion people suffering from chronic disease, only one point nine zero million patients per

41
00:04:52.260 --> 00:05:00.260
year get to participate in clinical trials annually. That's zero point zero seven nine two percent.

42
00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:07.820
Half would volunteer if asked. You're turning away ninety-nine point six percent of willing participants.

43
00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:19.220
On Democracy. A Princeton study found zero percent correlation between what the public wants and what policies get enacted.

44
00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:29.940
Zero. Not "low." Not "disappointing." Zero. Your democracy has the same correlation with your preferences as a coin flip

45
00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:38.860
has with your breakfast order. When military contractors want one hundred billion dollars, they spend fifty-five million

46
00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:45.320
dollars lobbying for it. That's a one thousand eight hundred thirteen percent return on investment.

47
00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.960
When you want healthcare, you have approximately zero dollars to lobby with.

48
00:05:51.620 --> 00:06:00.060
You spent it all on healthcare. Or you're dead, (which significantly reduces your lobbying capacity.) Meanwhile, the people

49
00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:07.500
who regulate industries used to work for those industries. They'll work for them again after they're done "regulating."

50
00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:16.920
(It's called the revolving door, and it spins in one direction: toward money.) On the Fixed Pie.

51
00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:25.400
Money isn't real, but resources are. Earth has 8 billion human brains.

52
00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:30.240
Every M.I.T. graduate building missiles is not curing cancer.

53
00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:35.800
Every brilliant physicist designing warheads is not designing M.R.I.

54
00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:43.280
machines. You have a fixed number of geniuses. You are using them to build things that kill other geniuses.

55
00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:51.920
Switzerland spends zero point seven percent of G.D.P. on military and has ninety-three thousand dollars G.D.P.

56
00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:58.220
per capita. America spends three point five percent and has seventy-six thousand dollars.

57
00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:03.060
The solution isn't to print more money for medical research.

58
00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:10.260
The solution is to change the ratio. Take money from the killing budget, give it to the not-dying budget.

59
00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:19.080
This is called "arithmetic," (which is apparently a controversial field of mathematics.) What This Means.

60
00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:28.060
One hundred fifty thousand humans die daily from disease and aging, many eventually avoidable.

61
00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:33.900
Two point seven two trillion dollars spent annually on weapons.

62
00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:41.420
Sixty-seven point five billion dollars spent annually on curing all diseases combined.

63
00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:46.500
Six hundred four weapons-to-clinical-trials spending ratio.

64
00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:54.880
Zero diseases cured in fifty years. Zero percent correlation between public preferences and policy.

65
00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:02.660
You are dying while reading this. If this seems bad, that's because you're paying attention.

66
00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:09.200
The good news is you're going to fix it. The bad news is it requires doing things.

67
00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:19.320
The weird news is you'll get rich doing it. What's Next. The following chapters explain each problem in detail: The Daily

